# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# .editorconfig requires `end_of_line = lf`, but Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true and checks files out as CRLF. `dotnet format
# --verify-no-changes` inspects the working copy, so without this file every
# Windows contributor sees hundreds of spurious ENDOFLINE errors on code they
# never touched, and line-ending churn leaks into unrelated diffs.
#
# Text files are stored as LF in the repository and checked out as LF on every
# platform, which matches both .editorconfig and the CI formatting check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pfx binary
*.snk binary

# Windows-only scripts need CRLF to run reliably.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
